// Starburst: fireworks over a hilltop town, built from free particles and light.
//
// Each rocket is a thin trail of flame painted at its head as it climbs out of
// a street between the houses, slowing near the top and leaning a little
// downwind; the flame lights the walls it passes. At the top a shell is a ring
// of hot star material painted in the air and blown apart in the same tick by
// one explosion at its center. An air burst throws each cell straight out from
// the center as a free particle with a fixed-point velocity, so the ring opens
// as a round burst; the blast's white flash lights the whole town for a moment
// and throws a few ember sparks. The flash and fire of the blast are cleared a
// few ticks later, after their light has gone out, so a burst leaves no
// ball of smoke behind; the stars are particles and fly on.
//
// The stars arc and fall under real gravity (9.84 m/s^2) and cool in flight,
// and their colour is their temperature. Gold stars are molten glass at
// 1,700 C: they open white-gold, fade through gold and orange, freeze to glass
// shards at 1,400 C and go on cooling, so they are dull red by the time they
// come down on the roofs. White stars are the same glass heated to 2,000 C.
// Lava stars burn orange-red and redden toward their freezing point. Double
// and triple shells break their inner rings a tick later and slower. Each
// burst's power is set from its height so its highest stars stay inside the
// top of the frame. No acid is used and no blast reaches the town: brick,
// torches and the hillside soil are all intact at the end.
//
// Spent stars that come down in the town are swept away: every quarter second
// the open air just above the roofs, the streets and the hillside is cleared
// (and the chimney mouths, so the chimney fires keep burning). The world runs
// 640 cells past the right edge of the frame, so the chimney and rocket smoke
// that the wind (3) carries off drifts out of view instead of piling against
// the edge.
//
// Timeline: quiet night; one gold shell over the keep (2.5 s); single and
// paired shells left and right in gold, white, orange and double rings
// (5.5-16 s); a crescendo of nine shells (18-21 s); a gold triple break over
// the keep with white flanks (23 s) whose stars rain red on the roofs; three
// small low shells as a coda (24.5 s); the last sparks die out as the camera
// eases in. The event lines are generated by a script.
[scene]
name = starburst
description = Fireworks over a hilltop town: rings of molten metal, glass and lava burst into free particles that cool from white-gold through orange to red in flight and light the roofs below.
bounds = 0 -760 1600 100
seed = 0x5b57
wind = 3
ticks = 1700

